    "Notebook" -> "0572c525-0bd8-462f-a519-7d7bc643835c"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\n## Support for Local LLMs in Assistant\nSome of you are \
using our old plugin that allows editing the notebook cells in automated mode \
using GPT models.\n\nBefore we restricted ourselves to OpenAI's `gpt-4*` \
models, however, some OSS and freeware solutions emerged on the market. We \
patched our API to be able to work with locally running LLM servers such as \
*Ollama*.\n\n![](/attachments/qwenWindow-685.png)\n\nThe only requirements \
are:\n\n- The completion API must be compatible with the OpenAI v1 API (this \
is usually the case for most models/LLM servers).\n- Support for \
plugins/tools.\n\n:::note\nLocal LLMs performance is strongly depend on your \
machine/model specs.\n:::\n\n...and we also fixed unicode issue \|01f642", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "c2e278aa-e447-4aba-9bf7-d783e6c2edb5", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "0572c525-0bd8-462f-a519-7d7bc643835c"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "## Support for Local LLMs in Assistant\nSome of you are using \
our old plugin that allows editing the notebook cells in automated mode using \
GPT models.\n\nBefore we restricted ourselves to OpenAI's `gpt-4*` models, \
however, some OSS and freeware solutions emerged on the market. We patched \
our API to be able to work with locally running LLM servers such as \
*Ollama*.\n\n![](/attachments/qwenWindow-685.png)\n\nThe only requirements \
are:\n\n- The completion API must be compatible with the OpenAI v1 API (this \
is usually the case for most models/LLM servers).\n- Support for \
plugins/tools.\n\n:::note\nLocal LLMs performance is strongly depend on your \
machine/model specs.\n:::\n\n...and we also fixed unicode issue \|01f642", 
    "Display" -> "markdown", "Hash" -> 
     "1d9f9b9e-10eb-4233-b61a-80e0b9d9280a", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "0572c525-0bd8-462f-a519-7d7bc643835c"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\n## AnimationRate\nWe fixed the missing feature of \
`RefreshRate` and `AnimationRate`:", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "c72f9090-0d94-437b-81d2-6ecf2e949d7d", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "0572c525-0bd8-462f-a519-7d7bc643835c"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "## AnimationRate\nWe fixed the missing feature of \
`RefreshRate` and `AnimationRate`:", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "e4307014-32f6-478d-b571-c4c070e4659d", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "0572c525-0bd8-462f-a519-7d7bc643835c"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "Animate[Graphics3D[Sphere[{0,0,1.0-(*SpB[*)Power[Cos[z](*|*),\
(*|*)2](*]SpB*)}, 0.1]], {z,0,10.0}, AnimationRate->0.03, RefreshRate->30]", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "8858d334-61d3-4453-b31b-1f350880b33b", "Invisible" -> False, 
